---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site.mjs';
---

<Base title="About" description="What this project is, what it is for, and how it is built in public.">
  <section>
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <h1>About</h1>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          This is a cycle-accurate 6502 and 65C02 core in C#, and the aim of implementing as many 6502-family machines as
          possible on it, each one proven. It is built in public: the design, the plan, the code and a journal of every
          step are in <a href={SITE.repo}>the repository</a>.
        </p>
        <h2>What proven means</h2>
        <p>
          The core is checked against recorded data from the real chip, against whole programs that check their own
          results, and against a model of the chip's transistors. A machine counts as implemented only when it runs in
          the browser and passes an automated test in CI. Where the work knowingly differs from a reference, that is
          written down on the <a href="/status/">status page</a>.
        </p>
        <h2>Nothing typed by hand</h2>
        <p>
          The figures on the home and status pages are read from the test results of the latest build and from dated
          measurements. The build fails if a figure is missing.
        </p>
        <h2>Illustrations</h2>
        <p>
          The images here were generated. They are illustrations, captioned as such, and none is used as evidence. The
          die is a plausible one drawn by a model, not the 6502's real layout.
        </p>
        <h2>Licence</h2>
        <p>MIT. No ROM, no game and no third-party test program is committed to the repository.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
